tm: Project TM, writing as claude for jace in session s1
Scheme default: types epic, story, task, bug, sub_task, spike, design
  statuses: triage (triage), todo (todo), in_progress (active), in_review (active), done (done), cancelled (cancelled)
  required: type, title, status
Remember (tm remember "..." adds one):
  check  Run mise run check before a commit  (jace, under a minute ago)
Waiting on jace (1): ask them, then tm answer KEY "..." records each reply:
  TM-1  todo  none  asked
    claude asked under a minute ago: Which way?
      options: 1. left  2. right
      the asking session resumes with: cd [repo] && claude -r s0
  Claude deletes a session unused for 30 days by default, so an old one may not resume.
Handed to you (tm start KEY takes one):
  TM-2  todo  none  handed  (from codex, no expiry)
    Pick this up; the tests pass
Your Claims:
  TM-3  todo  none  mine  (Claim [mine], no expiry)
Held by your other sessions:
  TM-4  todo  none  other  (session s2, no expiry)
Your lapsed Claims (another Agent may take these; tm heartbeat KEY takes one back):
  TM-5  todo  none  lapsed  (Claim [lapsed], lapsed [lapsed at])
Path Claims on your changes (1):
  TM-6  codex for jace covers notes.txt
Short-lists (tm next takes the first that can start):
  next-up (2 Issues)
    next  TM-9  todo  none  ready 1
          TM-10  todo  none  ready 2
In progress (1):
  TM-7  in_progress  none  started
Ready (8):
  TM-5  todo  none  lapsed
  TM-8  todo  none  mentioned
  TM-11  todo  none  ready 3
  2 on Short-lists, passed over: tm ready marks them
  and 3 more: tm ready
Notifications (1 unread, tm notifications lists them): jace on TM-8: @claude a long mention a long mention a long mention a lo…
Habits (tm guide has the rest):
  tm start KEY when work starts
  after a merge: git fetch, then tm git scan moves what it closed to done
  your writes renew your Claims; a person's tm setup claude or codex adds hooks that heartbeat between them
  the description holds the current plan; tm edit changes it
  tm comment KEY for progress, what was learned and changes of plan
